# Violent Urge's delirium is counted as it resolves (CR 608.2c): Wheel of Fortune puts Black Lotus (artifact), itself (sorcery) and an
# Island (land) into Bot1's graveyard - three card types. Violent Urge is an instant, so it would make a fourth the moment it is
# put into the graveyard, but while it resolves it is still on the stack (CR 608.2n puts it there after), so the Ornithopter gets
# +1/+0 and first strike only and, attacking unblocked, deals 1 damage (the other scenario, with four types, deals 2). The
# graveyard has no creature card: the Ornithopter drawn for the Wheel stays in the library.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Wheel of Fortune
Ornithopter
Island
Island
Island
Violent Urge
Mountain
Mountain
Island x4
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Wheel of Fortune.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Wheel of Fortune; Island; Island; Island; Black Lotus
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Violent Urge.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = FirstStrike; Flying
? Bot2.Life = 19

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = FirstStrike; Flying
